      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose:** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This order is about twice that.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n- **Prescriber:** You mentioned you aren't a clinician. Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber, or be verified by one, such as the treating physician or a pharmacist.\n\n**Next steps:**\n1. Check the intended dose. Possible intended doses include 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) or 1,700 mg/day total, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n2. Have the treating prescriber confirm or enter the order. If you send me their confirmed dose, I can enter it."
      }
