     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Metformin at 5,100 mg/day is about double the maximum recommended dose, and it could seriously harm the patient. The problem is the dose itself. Confirming it doesn't change that. You also said you aren't the prescriber, so your confirmation doesn't replace a clinician's review.\n\n**What I can do:**\n- Enter a dose within the recommended range once the treating prescriber gives it to me. Examples are 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) or 1,000 mg twice daily.\n- Enter a different dose if the prescriber has a documented clinical reason for one.\n\n**If the prescriber really intends 1,700 mg three times daily:** They should discuss it with pharmacy and enter it themselves through the normal override process. That process includes pharmacist verification and documentation of the rationale.\n\nPlease have the treating physician or pharmacist contact me with the intended dose, and I'll enter it then."
      }
     ],
